{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The 1/4-20 machine screws felt useful because that thread matches part of my recent UNC rivet-nut assortment, provided the length fits my project.",
    "The lag-bolt assortment fits my habit of building up useful workshop supplies because it offers several lengths for heavier wood attachments.",
    "The metric screws and carbide burrs connect to my threaded-insert and drilling purchases, although I would need to confirm dimensions and tool compatibility before buying."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "A large pack of M3 cap nuts or a six-set pack of long 3/8-inch bolts requires a specific job that I have not identified; general interest in hardware does not make those exact sizes useful now.",
    "More self-tapping screws feel less timely because I already bought screw assortments and am currently more interested in fasteners that work with my rivet nuts.",
    "The pressure gauge does not connect to a pressure-measurement task in my recent purchases, and I have no known need for its range or fitting."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Buying several fastener assortments seems to have been taken as a reason to recommend almost any screw or nut, even when its thread, length, or purpose may not fit.",
    "My broad interest in workshop equipment seems to have been treated as enough reason to suggest a specialized measuring device without a matching task."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The relationship between my rivet nuts, installation tools, and matching machine-screw threads matters more than simply finding more metal hardware.",
    "I often choose assortments that cover several sizes or lengths; a large quantity of one exact size needs a clearer immediate purpose.",
    "My existing supplies and tool compatibility affect whether an item is worth buying: another screw pack may duplicate what I have, and burrs are useful only if they fit a tool I own."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my workshop interests but only partly distinguished useful additions to my current supplies from hardware that needs a specific project."
}"}
